//****************************************************************************
// $Module type: Class Package
// $Module name: cWinAPICatalogStore
// $Author     : Nils Svedmyr, RDC Tools International, <mailto:support@rdctools.com>
// Web-site    : http://www.rdctools.com
// Created     : 2026-08-26
//
// Description : The Windows API catalogues as editable JSON: loads Data\WinAPICatalog.json
//               and Data\WinAPIStructCatalog.json over the compiled-in seed. The seed is the
//               floor - a missing or unreadable file degrades to the seed, never to a broken
//               tool. Carries the load/refresh latch and the lookups the funclib consumes.
//
// This code is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY;
// without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.
//****************************************************************************
Use RefactorConstants.h.pkg
Use RefactorFileIO.pkg   // rfOpenInput / rfOpenOutput / Read_Block - the same channel I/O the rules JSON uses
Use cJsonObject.pkg

/*  cWinAPICatalogStore - the Windows API catalogues as editable JSON.

    THE COMPILED SEED IS THE FLOOR, the JSON is where the catalogue GROWS. WinAPICatalog.inc and its
    two siblings are still #Included into cBaseFuncLib and still ship in the exe; this only decides
    which rows the funclib ends up holding. A missing or unreadable file therefore degrades to
    "the seed", never to a broken tool - which is why the seed was not simply replaced.

    WHY IT HAD TO BECOME EDITABLE. The catalogue's only real problem is size: 56 API entries against
    the 1,310 distinct entry points found across the workspaces on C:. Adding entries must cost an
    edit, not a build, or it will not happen.

    ONE LOADER FOR THREE CATALOGUES, because all three are String[] of "|"-packed rows. What differs
    is how many leading fields make a row's IDENTITY - dll|entry for an API, the NAME alone for a
    struct or a bitness split - so that count is a parameter.

    THE MERGE RULE IS THE POINT, and it differs from DeepScanRules.json. There a user contributes a
    TOGGLE, merged across by DS number. Here a user contributes whole ROWS, so on a version bump the
    seed replaces the rows it owns (a corrected prototype must actually reach an existing install)
    and every row the seed does NOT own is carried across. Without that, a version bump would delete
    a user's additions silently - not noticed until something quietly stopped converting.

    ALL PATHS ARE EXPLICIT PARAMETERS so the unit tests never touch the real files, exactly as
    cDeepScanner does.
*/
// A row's identity: its first iKeyFields "|"-separated fields, lowercased. Two rows with the same key are
// the same entry however their payload differs, which is what lets a seed row replace a user's stale copy of
// it while leaving a genuinely new row alone. The one rule - the store's merge test exercises it through
// _RowKey below, the harvester's merge (cWin32ProjectionHarvester) calls it directly.
Function WinApiRowKey Global String sRow Integer iKeyFields Returns String
    String sOut sRest
    Integer i iPos

    Move "" to sOut
    Move sRow to sRest
    For i from 1 to iKeyFields
        Move (Pos("|", sRest)) to iPos
        If (iPos = 0) Begin
            If (sOut = "") ;
                Function_Return (Lowercase(Trim(sRest)))
            Function_Return (Lowercase(sOut + sRest))
        End
        Move (sOut + Left(sRest, iPos)) to sOut
        Move (Right(sRest, (Length(sRest) - iPos))) to sRest
    Loop
    Function_Return (Lowercase(sOut))
End_Function

Class cWinAPICatalogStore is a cObject

    // Why the last load returned nothing, or "" when it was fine. Read by the caller so an empty
    // catalogue can announce itself instead of passing for "nothing to convert".
    Procedure Construct_Object
        Forward Send Construct_Object
        Property String psLastProblem ""
    End_Procedure

    /* DFRefactor's OWN Data folder - pOrgWS, never pTargetWS. These catalogues are knowledge about
       Windows, not about the workspace being refactored, so one copy serves every target. Returns
       "" when the app has no resolved own-workspace yet (which happens during keyword-init on a
       fresh start); the caller reads that as "no JSON layer" and uses the seed. */
    Function CatalogJsonPath String sFileName Returns String
        String sData
        Handle hoWS

        If (ghoApplication = 0) ;
            Function_Return ""
        // phoWorkspace, NOT pOrgWS. Both name DFRefactor's own Data folder, but pOrgWS lives on
        // cRefactorApplication only - and the DFUnit runner is built on plain cApplication, where
        // reading it raises err 98. This resolver has to answer in both, so it uses the accessor
        // both have; it is the same one ModAnalyzerRecipesJsonPath reads for the same reason.
        Get phoWorkspace of ghoApplication to hoWS
        If (hoWS = 0) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Get psDataPath of hoWS to sData
        If (Trim(sData) = "") ;
            Function_Return ""
        Function_Return (vFolderFormat(sData) + sFileName)
    End_Function

    // The rule WinApiRowKey states, as the method the merge test exercises.
    Function _RowKey String sRow Integer iKeyFields Returns String
        Function_Return (WinApiRowKey(sRow, iKeyFields))
    End_Function

    Function _ReadCatalogFile String sPath Returns tWinAPICatalogFile
        Handle hoJson
        tWinAPICatalogFile TheFile

        Get rfParseJsonFile sPath to hoJson
        If (hoJson <> 0) Begin
            Get JsonToDataType of hoJson to TheFile
            Send Destroy of hoJson
        End
        Function_Return TheFile
    End_Function

    Procedure WriteCatalogAtVersion String[] asRows String sPath Integer iVersion
        Handle hoJson
        UChar[] ucJson
        Integer iCh
        tWinAPICatalogFile TheFile

        If (Trim(sPath) = "") ;
            Procedure_Return
        Move iVersion to TheFile.iVersion
        Move asRows   to TheFile.asRows
        Get Create (RefClass(cJsonObject)) to hoJson
        Send DataTypeToJson of hoJson TheFile
        Set peWhiteSpace of hoJson to jpWhitespace_Pretty
        Get StringifyUtf8 of hoJson to ucJson
        Send Destroy of hoJson
        Get rfOpenOutput sPath to iCh
        If (iCh < 0) ;
            Procedure_Return
        Write channel iCh ucJson
        Send rfCloseOutput iCh
    End_Procedure

    Procedure WriteCatalog String[] asRows String sPath
        Send WriteCatalogAtVersion asRows sPath CI_WinAPICatalogVersion
    End_Procedure

    /* The rows every consumer reads. THE FILE IS THE ONLY COPY - there is no compiled seed behind
       it any more, and that single fact shapes everything below.

       WHY NO SEED. The catalogue is hand-curated data, not logic, and it exists to be EXTENDED
       without a rebuild. Keeping a compiled copy as well would have meant two tracked originals
       that drift, and worse: on a version bump the seed would replace a row the user had edited,
       which is the feature fighting itself. Git is the source of truth, and it holds a tracked
       .json exactly as well as it held a .inc (Nils, 2026-08-26).

       SO IT NEVER REWRITES THE FILE ON A VERSION MISMATCH. With a seed, a bump meant "reseed and
       merge". With none, an older iVersion means only that the file predates a format change -
       and rewriting it from nothing would destroy the very rows it is asked to load. Old rows are
       returned as they are; migrating a format is a deliberate act, not a side effect of reading.

       A MISSING OR UNREADABLE FILE IS REPORTED, not shrugged off. It degrades safely - every
       converter refuses an API it cannot find - but silently, and "no conversions" reads exactly
       like "nothing needed converting". psLastProblem carries the reason so a caller can say it. */
    Function LoadCatalog String sPath Returns String[]
        tWinAPICatalogFile TheFile
        String[] asNone
        Boolean bExists

        Set psLastProblem to ""
        If (Trim(sPath) = "") Begin
            Set psLastProblem to "No workspace resolved yet, so no catalogue path could be built."
            Function_Return asNone
        End
        Get vFilePathExists sPath to bExists
        If (bExists = False) Begin
            Set psLastProblem to ("Catalogue file not found: " + sPath ;
                + " - every API lookup will come back empty until it is restored.")
            Function_Return asNone
        End
        Get _ReadCatalogFile sPath to TheFile
        If (SizeOfArray(TheFile.asRows) = 0) Begin
            Set psLastProblem to ("Catalogue file holds no rows (unreadable or empty): " + sPath)
            Function_Return asNone
        End
        If (TheFile.iVersion <> CI_WinAPICatalogVersion) ;
            Set psLastProblem to ("Catalogue file is format version " + String(TheFile.iVersion) ;
                + ", this build expects " + String(CI_WinAPICatalogVersion) ;
                + " - rows loaded as they are; the file is NOT rewritten, it is the only copy.")
        Function_Return TheFile.asRows
    End_Function

End_Class
